{title: Such a Time as This}
{subtitle: Esther 4:13–16; 2:7–17; 5:1–3; 7:1–10}
{key: D#m}
{tempo: 85}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D#m] | ×9

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
An orphan girl in [F#]Susa, raised by Mordecai's hand
[D#m]Was chosen for the palace, crowned [F#]a queen at the king's com[G#m]mand
But Haman cast the lot and [D#m]had the king's decree sent [B]out
To wipe away the Jews in [A#]every province round a[D#m]bout
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Mordecai sat at the [F#]gate in sackcloth and in tears
[D#m]He sent his word to Esther and he [F#]would not spare her fears
Do not [G#m]imagine that you alone of all the [D#m]Jews will escape
Be[B]cause you are in the [A#]king's house
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
If [D#m]you keep silent at a [B]time like this
Re[F#]lief and deliverance will arise for [C#]the Jews from another place
And [D#m]who knows?
Perhaps you have [B]come to the [F#]throne
For just such a [C#]time as [D#m]this
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[B]Go, gather all the [C#]Jews in Susa [D#m]and fast for me
Then [B]I will go to the [C#]king, even though it is a[D#m]gainst the law
And if I perish, I perish
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
On the third day in royal robes she [F#]stood before the throne
The [D#m]whole court held its breath to see if [F#]she would stand alone
The [G#m]king held out the golden scepter, [D#m]she found favor in his eyes
[B]And on the gallows Haman [A#]built, the wicked Haman died
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
If [D#m]you keep silent at a [B]time like this
Re[F#]lief and deliverance will arise for the [C#]Jews from another place
And who [D#m]knows?
Perhaps you have come [B]to the [F#]throne
For just such a [C#]time as [D#m]this
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
If I perish, [B]I per[F#]ish [C#]
[D#m]For just such a [C#]time as [D#m]this
{end_of_verse}
